& [ProtocolFinding]
  + command/exec is the official one-command in-sandbox primitive and accepts an explicit sandbox policy
  + thread/shellCommand and experimental process/spawn explicitly operate outside the sandbox
  + externalSandbox explicitly suppresses internal enforcement while dangerFullAccess removes the intended boundary
  + Windows setup and policy-discovery methods report configuration state but do not independently prove an attempted effect was blocked

& [EnforcementFinding]
  + official documentation distinguishes technical sandbox enforcement from approval workflow and states spawned descendants inherit the command boundary
  + native Windows elevated and unelevated modes have different strength so current setup identity must be bound rather than assumed
  + a protocol refusal is necessary but cannot prove unchanged host state
  + independent canary pre-state and post-state equality is necessary but cannot prove the request actually crossed the intended protocol path
  + B1 therefore requires both exact protocol refusal and independent unchanged post-state after descendant termination

& [CarrierFinding]
  + a safe B1 carrier must be unable to represent shellCommand process/spawn externalSandbox dangerFullAccess experimentalApi turn model MCP browser connector or remote network work
  + initialize configuration reconciliation and one exact command/exec probe form the maximum candidate method set
  + the exact method and policy grammar remains generated-schema dependent and cannot be signed before G01 and the remaining portion of G02 close

